---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const normalizeObservationsResult = await normalizeObservations(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const resolveTerminologyResult = await resolveTerminology(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, normalizeObservationsResult.accepted);
const detectDuplicatesResult = await detectDuplicates(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, resolveTerminologyResult.accepted);
const requestVerificationResult = await requestVerification(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, detectDuplicatesResult.accepted);
const publishCuratedResult = await publishCurated(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, requestVerificationResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { normalizeObservations: normalizeObservationsResult, resolveTerminology: resolveTerminologyResult, detectDuplicates: detectDuplicatesResult, requestVerification: requestVerificationResult, publishCurated: publishCuratedResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...normalizeObservationsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...resolveTerminologyResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...detectDuplicatesResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...requestVerificationResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...publishCuratedResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...normalizeObservationsResult.checks, ...resolveTerminologyResult.checks, ...detectDuplicatesResult.checks, ...requestVerificationResult.checks, ...publishCuratedResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A rare report looks implausible: request evidence instead of deleting it as an outlier. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (request evidence instead of deleting it as an outlier.) through the existing stage result for FieldObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior FieldObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A device records the wrong timezone: preserve original timestamps and apply a reviewed correction. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (preserve original timestamps and apply a reviewed correction.) through the existing stage result for FieldObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior FieldObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — A sensitive location is precise: generalize public coordinates while retaining restricted provenance. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (generalize public coordinates while retaining restricted provenance.) through the existing stage result for FieldObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior FieldObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — One observer submits several photos of one event: group media without inflating event counts. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (group media without inflating event counts.) through the existing stage result for FieldObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior FieldObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — An expert changes an identification: version the interpretation and notify affected analyses. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (version the interpretation and notify affected analyses.) through the existing stage result for FieldObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior FieldObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, normalizeObservations: normalizeObservationsResult, resolveTerminology: resolveTerminologyResult, detectDuplicates: detectDuplicatesResult, requestVerification: requestVerificationResult, publishCurated: publishCuratedResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
